                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued October 21 at 7:10AM MST until October 21 at 7:30AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "At 710 AM MST, a severe thunderstorm was located 6 miles east of\nYarnell, or 23 miles southwest of Prescott, moving northeast at 50\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Two inch hail and 60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail\ndamage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect wind\ndamage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nYarnell, Wilhoit, Peeples Valley, Kirkland, Potato Patch, Skull\nValley, Copper Basin, Hawkins, Palace Station, Stanton, Kirkland\nJunction, Walnut Grove, Granite Mountain Hotshots Memorial State\nPark, Mt. Union and Weaver Peak.\n\nThis includes State Route 89 between mile markers 272 and 304.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nUpper Wolf Creek Group Campground, Lower Wolf Creek Campground and\nWolf Creek Falls.\n\nThis includes the following swimming holes...\nWolf Creek Falls.",
                "instruction": "Anyone outdoors should move to shelter inside a well-built structure\nand stay away from windows. This storm is capable of producing\ndangerous hail and damaging winds.",
